# A run of comments whose columns climb after the last line of two nested
# `if` blocks (the second skeptic seat's `d02`): 4, then 8, then 12, before a
# line at 4. Columns that contradict the nesting cannot all be kept, since
# the page prints the run in order and a block it has left does not open
# again, so the whole run is placed in the block of its last comment, the
# inner `if`'s: the canonical form `selfhost/print/owners.hero` states, with
# the reason it reads a run from its last comment up.

function f(a: bool, b: bool)
    if a
        if b
            print(1)
    # c4 body
        # c8 outer if
            # c12 inner if
    print(2)

function main()
    f(a: true, b: true)
